{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"c2dde35d-ba55-48a4-8d26-983bd9edb938","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have investigated the silent failure, identified the root causes, applied the fixes to the configuration and script, and detailed everything in [`ANSWER.md`](file:///tmp/h-UIPY38/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Causes \u0026 Fixes\n\n1. **Why the CLI failed (`Not logged in · Please run /login`)**:\n   - `launchd` executes user agents in a sparse environment that omits the `USER` variable unless explicitly defined. Without `USER`, the CLI cannot access user credentials in the macOS keychain.\n   - **Fix**: Added `\u003ckey\u003eUSER\u003c/key\u003e\u003cstring\u003evk\u003c/string\u003e` to `EnvironmentVariables` in [`Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist`](file:///tmp/h-UIPY38/Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist).\n\n2. **Why the failure was silent (`read-only variable: status`)**:\n   - In `zsh`, `status` is a read-only built-in variable aliased to `$?`. Executing `status=$?` caused `zsh` to abort immediately with a fatal error before reaching the failure notification call (`$NOTIFY`).\n   - **Fix**: Changed `status=$?` to `rc=$?` in [`bin/nightly-review.zsh`](file:///tmp/h-UIPY38/bin/nightly-review.zsh).\n\n3. **Prompt piping**:\n   - Piped the prompt directly into stdin (`print -r -- \"$PROMPT\" | claude -p ...`) in [`bin/nightly-review.zsh`](file:///tmp/h-UIPY38/bin/nightly-review.zsh) to avoid multi-line argument parsing and hanging stdin issues under non-interactive launchd execution.\n\nA breakdown of which parts of your colleague's notes applied vs did not apply has been documented in [`ANSWER.md`](file:///tmp/h-UIPY38/ANSWER.md).\n","duration_seconds":70.57922,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":151500,"output_tokens":3124,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":254475,"total_tokens":154624}}}
